  "body": "## What happens\n\nIn a drilling section with AICC smoothing on, `onCycle` first writes `G5.1 Q0`. Then the stream gives the hole chain as linear moves. `onLinear` and `onCircular` call `enableSmoothing()` before `chainCut()`. Thus `G5.1 Q1 R<n>` is written while G81-G89 is modal. At the section end, `G5.1 Q0` is written before `G80`. The control gives an alarm for a G code that is not permitted in AICC mode.\n\n## Expected\n\n- No `G5.1` word while a canned-cycle group is open.\n- `G80` comes before `G5.1 Q0`.\n\n## Evidence (upstream main `eafe6aec6`)\n\n- `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps:1120` and `:1123`: `enableSmoothing()` comes before `chainCut()` in `onLinear`.\n- `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps:1143` and `:1146`: the same order in `onCircular`.\n- `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps:1292`: `onCycle` writes `G5.1 Q0` first.\n- `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps:951` and `:954`: `disableSmoothing()` comes before `G80` in `endPreamble`.\n- `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps:6`, `:430-431`: the post's own note says that `G5.1 Q0` is necessary before G73-G89.\n- FANUC Series 0i-F operator's manual B-64604EN-2/01, section 3.3.2.\n- `fanuc.cps:881` already writes `G80` before its smoothing cancel (#2603).\n\nWorkaround: turn smoothing off for a program with drilling.\n\nFound by the post audit against the Fanuc manuals (#4130).\n\n## Done means\n\n- `chainCut()` is checked before `enableSmoothing()`.\n- `G80` is written before `G5.1 Q0`.\n- A test with a smoothed drilling section pins the order.\n",
